    {
      "title": "Gather your payment receipt and booking records",
      "detail": "Collect your payment receipt for Rs. 2,000 paid to CleanHome on 2 October 2026. Also gather your booking confirmation, service terms, and screenshots of all unacknowledged messages sent to CleanHome, as you noted these details are currently needed."
    },
    {
      "title": "Write to CleanHome's Grievance Officer",
      "detail": "Contact CleanHome in writing requesting a full refund of Rs. 2,000 for failing to provide the promised sofa cleaning service. Under the law, an e-commerce platform must have a grievance officer who acknowledges a consumer complaint within 48 hours and redresses it within one month [SRC:ECOM2020-R4-5] [SRC:ECOM2020-R4-4]. If CleanHome acts as an e-commerce marketplace, you may also ask them in writing for the seller's details [SRC:ECOM2020-R5-3-a]."
    },
    {
      "title": "Report the issue to the National Consumer Helpline",
      "detail": "If CleanHome does not respond or refund your Rs. 2,000, you can register a grievance with the National Consumer Helpline by calling toll-free 1915 (8 AM to 8 PM) or 1800114000, messaging WhatsApp at +918800001915, or using the web portal consumerhelpline.gov.in [SRC:NCH-CONTACT]."
    },
    {
      "title": "Consider filing a complaint with the District Consumer Commission",
      "detail": "If the matter remains unresolved, you may consider filing a consumer complaint against CleanHome for deficiency of service [SRC:CPA2019-S2-11]. Complaints must generally be filed within two years from when the issue arose [SRC:CPA2019-S69], and can be filed electronically through e-jagriti.gov.in [SRC:CPA2019-S35-1]. For your paid amount of Rs. 2,000, there is no filing fee for amounts up to Rs. 5 lakh [SRC:CDRC2023-R7-FEE]. The Commission may also suggest resolving the matter through mediation if both sides agree in writing [SRC:CPA2019-S37-1]."
    }
  ]
}
